<title>USA: CBOT October volume rises 6.8 percent year-on-year.</title>
<headline>CBOT October volume rises 6.8 percent year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade (CBOT) said its futures and options volume totalled 18,710,983 contracts in October, up 6.8 percent from 17,524,556 contracts traded in October 1995.</p>
<p>CBOT said volume in the first 10 months of 1996 rose 6.0 percent to 189,198,625 contracts from 178,550,566 contracts in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows, with volume for October 1996 and percentage change followed by October 1995 volume:  </p>
<p>All futures     13,628,604     + 2.1     13,343,806</p>
<p>  Agricultural   4,535,553     +12.4	4,036,914</p>
<p>  Financial	9,090,430     - 2.3	9,303,445</p>
<p>All options on</p>
<p>	 futures   5,082,379     +21.6	4,180,750</p>
<p>  Agricultural   1,421,335     +42.0	1,000,628</p>
<p>  Financial	3,659,523     +15.1	3,179,792</p>
<p>Futures (individual)</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     6,772,385     - 2.2	6,927,156</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes 1,494,695     + 2.4	1,459,737</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes    689,510     -10.4	  769,591</p>
<p>  Wheat		362,047     -23.4	  472,794</p>
<p>  Corn	     1,435,686     -11.0	1,613,217</p>
<p>  Soybeans	 1,695,553     +50.3	1,127,885</p>
<p>  Soymeal	    561,126     +29.4	  449,009</p>
<p>  Soyoil	     414,018     +30.5	  317,201</p>
<p>Options</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     2,716,250     +18.1	2,299,006</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes   670,115     +16.1	  577,299</p>
<p>  Corn		 605,685     +30.1	  465,591</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   595,768     +83.3	  325,029</p>
<p>-- Chicago Derivatives Desk (312) 408 8750</p>
</text>
